{
  "schema_version": "argument_graph/0.1",
  "example_id": "persuade:671D0569C835",
  "root": "x7",
  "units": [
    {
      "id": "x1",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 27,
      "text": "Dear Florida State Senator,",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x2",
      "start": 29,
      "end": 129,
      "text": "Every 4 years, many people vote for a president they think will lead the United States to greatness;",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x3",
      "start": 130,
      "end": 227,
      "text": "some, however, don't know that they are voting for the Electoral College to vote on their choise.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x4",
      "start": 228,
      "end": 302,
      "text": "This act of using the Electoral College is, by definition, not democratic.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x5",
      "start": 303,
      "end": 397,
      "text": "Didn't our founding fathers create this country promising democracy and people representation?",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x6",
      "start": 398,
      "end": 407,
      "text": "They did,",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x7",
      "start": 408,
      "end": 459,
      "text": "and that is why the Electoral College must crumble.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x8",
      "start": 460,
      "end": 537,
      "text": "Florida State Senator, we need to change how our country votes on its leader;",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x9",
      "start": 538,
      "end": 604,
      "text": "we need to use popular vote for the president of the United States",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x10",
      "start": 605,
      "end": 644,
      "text": "because this method is more democratic,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x11",
      "start": 645,
      "end": 710,
      "text": "the people representing the  Electoral College are flawed humans,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x12",
      "start": 711,
      "end": 784,
      "text": "and the nature of this type of election forces some states to be ignored.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x13",
      "start": 785,
      "end": 866,
      "text": "Florida State Senator, you must take action against the flawed Electoral College!",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x14",
      "start": 868,
      "end": 958,
      "text": "Because of the function of the Electoral College, the people aren't truly represented for.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x15",
      "start": 959,
      "end": 1081,
      "text": "According to Source 2, the voters--the ones supposedly voting for our new president--vote for a group of electors instead.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x16",
      "start": 1082,
      "end": 1160,
      "text": "Due to the power of the Electoral Colleg, electors can vote for any candidate.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x17",
      "start": 1161,
      "end": 1219,
      "text": "This process we have every 4 years is truly un-democratic.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x18",
      "start": 1220,
      "end": 1314,
      "text": "For example, during the 2000 election, Al Gore was the candidate with the most popular votes--",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x19",
      "start": 1314,
      "end": 1397,
      "text": "this meant that the majority of the citizens of the U.S. wants him to be president.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x20",
      "start": 1398,
      "end": 1419,
      "text": "However, Al Gore lost",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x21",
      "start": 1420,
      "end": 1488,
      "text": "since the majority of electors from the Electoral College voted him.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x22",
      "start": 1489,
      "end": 1560,
      "text": "Lastly, in the case of a time, the lection will truly be un-democratic;",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x23",
      "start": 1561,
      "end": 1628,
      "text": "the House of Representatives will have to choose the new president.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x24",
      "start": 1629,
      "end": 1701,
      "text": "The people may allow continued usage of the imperfect Electoral College,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x25",
      "start": 1702,
      "end": 1739,
      "text": "but there is still one major problem:",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x26",
      "start": 1740,
      "end": 1810,
      "text": "the Electoral College is made up of flawed, easily manipulated humans.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x27",
      "start": 1812,
      "end": 1912,
      "text": "According to Source 1, the electors are made up of people chosen by the candidate's political party.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x28",
      "start": 1913,
      "end": 1987,
      "text": "Immediately, these electors can easily decide on the candidate to vote on;",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x29",
      "start": 1988,
      "end": 2054,
      "text": "it's just the matter of the amount of electors each candidate has.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x30",
      "start": 2055,
      "end": 2091,
      "text": "Also, the electors are human beings,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x31",
      "start": 2092,
      "end": 2144,
      "text": "and everyone knows that humans are flawed creatures.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x32",
      "start": 2145,
      "end": 2271,
      "text": "According to Source 2, electors have been replaced to be against the opposing candidate or wait until the last minute to vote.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x33",
      "start": 2272,
      "end": 2328,
      "text": "Although, according to Source 3, the electors are chosen",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x33b",
      "start": 2329,
      "end": 2349,
      "text": "and are given trust,",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x34",
      "start": 2350,
      "end": 2382,
      "text": "others can still influence them.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x35",
      "start": 2383,
      "end": 2479,
      "text": "Candidates or even political parties can influence the electors to vote for their chosen person.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x36",
      "start": 2480,
      "end": 2580,
      "text": "Lastly, Florida State Senator, the nature of the Electoral College forces some states to be ignored.",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x37",
      "start": 2582,
      "end": 2711,
      "text": "Florida State Senator, as you may know, the candidate for presidency usually go to the \"swing\" states to win \"the people's\" vote.",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x38",
      "start": 2712,
      "end": 2777,
      "text": "People, however, from the non-swing states are generally ignored.",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x39",
      "start": 2778,
      "end": 2894,
      "text": "During the 2000 election, 17 states weren't even able to see a candidate they are voting for the title of president.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x40",
      "start": 2895,
      "end": 2979,
      "text": "Although it is understandable that candidates go to the \"swing\" and populous states,",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x41",
      "start": 2980,
      "end": 3054,
      "text": "there is no excuse for ignoring thousands of people from the small states.",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x42",
      "start": 3055,
      "end": 3154,
      "text": "The president of the United States is the president for an entire country, not just a region of it.",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x43",
      "start": 3155,
      "end": 3254,
      "text": "Voters from the non-swing states will still want to see the candidate to decide on who to vote for,",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x44",
      "start": 3255,
      "end": 3311,
      "text": "even though they aren't voting for the actual candidate.",
      "role": "rebuttal",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x45",
      "start": 3312,
      "end": 3365,
      "text": "The Electoral College is imperfect and un-democratic!",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x46",
      "start": 3367,
      "end": 3438,
      "text": "In conclusion, the Electoral College and its electors must be disbanded",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x47",
      "start": 3439,
      "end": 3527,
      "text": "so that popular vote will be used in determining the new president of the United States.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x48",
      "start": 3528,
      "end": 3635,
      "text": "According to both Source 2 and 3, the process of voting a group of people to vote for you is un-democratic.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x49",
      "start": 3636,
      "end": 3753,
      "text": "Electors, the people making up th Electoral College, can be manipulated and coerced into voting a specific candidate.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x50",
      "start": 3754,
      "end": 3795,
      "text": "Lastly, non-swing states will be ignored;",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x51",
      "start": 3796,
      "end": 3830,
      "text": "this will anger and frustrate them",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x52",
      "start": 3831,
      "end": 3878,
      "text": "since not one candidate tried to persuade them.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x53",
      "start": 3879,
      "end": 4023,
      "text": "Florida State Senator, you must, in the best of your ability and then some, try to topple down the un-democratic roots of the Electoral College.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x54",
      "start": 4024,
      "end": 4124,
      "text": "The people, the ones who must truly decide on the president, will be immensely greatful towards you;",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x55",
      "start": 4125,
      "end": 4170,
      "text": "in a 2000 poll, 60% of the voters even stated",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x56",
      "start": 4171,
      "end": 4218,
      "text": "that they want a popular-vote type of election.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x57",
      "start": 4219,
      "end": 4325,
      "text": "Florida State Senator, I implore to you, abolish the Electoral College in the same manner as with slavery.",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "x58",
      "start": 4326,
      "end": 4353,
      "text": "Many people will thank you!",
      "role": "unannotated",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    }
  ],
